# Bloodline Motion Rules

## Core Motion Philosophy

Motion should feel:

- fast
- cinematic
- tactical
- controlled
- premium
- energetic

Avoid:
- playful motion
- floaty motion
- startup-style animation
- over-designed cinematic effects
- gimmicky interactions

---

## Motion Identity

The platform should move like:

```txt
Aggressive premium tattoo culture
```

NOT:
- futuristic gaming UI
- editorial fashion minimalism
- playful SaaS interfaces
- WebGL-heavy experiences

---

## Motion Density Rules

Motion should remain:
- selective
- intentional
- supportive

Avoid:
- animating everything
- constant movement
- competing motion systems
- visual overload

Motion should reinforce:
- focus
- hierarchy
- polish

---

## Timing Rules

Preferred duration range:

```txt
0.2s → 0.7s
```

### Hover Interactions

```txt
0.2s → 0.3s
```

### Section Reveals

```txt
0.45s → 0.7s
```

### Modal Transitions

```txt
0.3s → 0.5s
```

Avoid:
- extremely slow luxury timing
- hyper-fast jarring transitions

---

## Easing Rules

Preferred easing:

```txt
cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)
```

Avoid:
- bounce easing
- elastic easing
- cartoon-like transitions

---

## Allowed Motion Types

Allowed:

- fade reveal
- fade-up reveal
- stagger reveal
- subtle scale
- hover zoom
- overlay fade
- image depth transitions
- modal fade
- tactical CTA interaction

Motion should remain:
```txt
clean and controlled
```

---

## Forbidden Motion Types

Never introduce:

- bounce
- spin
- floating blobs
- excessive parallax
- scroll hijacking
- particle systems
- exaggerated 3D effects
- chaotic looping animations
- gimmicky hover effects

The platform should never feel:
```txt
playful or experimental
```

---

## Hero Motion Rules

Hero motion may include:
- subtle background motion
- layered reveal timing
- cinematic fades
- controlled image scaling

Avoid:
- dramatic animated typography
- distracting motion overload
- aggressive parallax systems

The hero must remain:
- readable
- premium
- performance-safe

---

## Scroll Animation Rules

Use:
- reveal-on-scroll
- stagger groups
- subtle section transitions

Avoid:
- cinematic scroll choreography
- complex scroll timelines
- heavy scroll-triggered rendering

Scroll motion should feel:
```txt
responsive and polished
```

---

## Hover Rules

Hover interactions should feel:
- responsive
- tactical
- premium

Allowed:
- slight scale
- border transition
- subtle glow
- overlay reveal

Avoid:
- dramatic zoom
- wobble
- elastic hover behavior
- decorative hover gimmicks

---

## CTA Motion Rules

CTA motion should:
- reinforce confidence
- feel energetic
- remain subtle

Allowed:
- slight scale
- glow enhancement
- opacity transition

Avoid:
- constant pulsing
- flashing CTA systems
- attention-spam animation

---

## Gallery Motion Rules

Gallery systems may use:
- image hover depth
- overlay transitions
- staggered reveal
- subtle zoom

Avoid:
- unstable layout animation
- exaggerated motion
- slow cinematic dragging

Gallery interaction should feel:
```txt
smooth and premium
```

---

## Modal Motion Rules

Modals should:
- appear quickly
- preserve focus
- feel intentional

Preferred:
- fade + scale combination
- overlay fade
- subtle depth transition

Avoid:
- oversized transitions
- sliding chaos
- theatrical animation

---

## Mobile Motion Rules

Mobile motion should prioritize:
- performance
- clarity
- responsiveness

Avoid:
- heavy animation payloads
- excessive mobile transforms
- CPU-intensive interactions

Mobile experience must remain:
```txt
fast and stable
```

---

## Accessibility Rules

Always support:
- `prefers-reduced-motion`
- motion-safe alternatives
- accessible timing

Non-essential motion should reduce gracefully.

Accessibility is mandatory.

---

## Performance Rules

Prefer:
- transform animations
- opacity transitions
- GPU-safe motion

Avoid:
- layout-thrashing animation
- expensive paint operations
- oversized animation libraries

Motion should never damage:
- LCP
- responsiveness
- scroll smoothness

---

## Motion Stack Rules

Approved motion stack:

```txt
Motion
CSS transitions
Tailwind animation utilities
```

Avoid introducing:
- unnecessary animation frameworks
- experimental rendering engines
- heavy 3D systems

---

## Reusability Rules

Motion should use:
- reusable wrappers
- reusable reveal systems
- reusable hover systems

Avoid:
- unique animation systems per section
- duplicated animation logic

Preferred structure:

```txt
components/motion/
```

---

## SEO Safety Rules

Motion must never:
- hide critical SEO content
- block rendering
- depend entirely on client hydration

SEO-critical content should remain:
- visible
- crawlable
- server-rendered

---

## AI Motion Safety Rules

AI-generated motion must:
- follow timing standards
- follow easing standards
- preserve performance
- preserve readability

Avoid:
- inventing random motion styles
- over-animating sections
- introducing disconnected animation language

---

## Forbidden Patterns

Never introduce:

- bounce animation
- floating blobs
- flashy cyberpunk motion
- giant parallax systems
- autoplay chaos
- spinning UI
- random easing systems
- cinematic overproduction

---

## Final Principle

Every motion decision should reinforce:

- confidence
- energy
- polish
- authority
- responsiveness
- premium positioning

If motion weakens readability, performance, trust, or clarity, do not implement it.